From 2e410e75965abbd21724585daaf4f91336dd71ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: oxjmo <oxjmo@localhost>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:50:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] OnePlus 6 (enchilada): Synaptics S3706 touch and the TLMM
 east tile

The touch screen answers on BLSP12 once its 2.8V (cmd-db ldoa28) and
1.8V VDDIO rails are up; both GPIOs live in the TLMM east tile, whose
base is not the node address the device tree prints but what the driver
of the south tile reads back from it -- writing the node address is what
bricked the phone five times. redwood_s3320.c maps each tile by name,
serves normalized samples to /dev/redwood-touch, and the loader pokes
the rails on the east tile as well.
